    "result_text": "All 62 tests pass, including the new `Cp50Tests`, with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent creates on `POST /api/owners`: when a request carries an `Idempotency-Key` header that has already been used to create an owner, the endpoint replays the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which the duplicate-identity check would otherwise reject with 409).\n\nI followed the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (per `AGENTS.md`), not Spring MVC. New pieces:\n\n**Pipeline changes** (`src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`)\n- Added `checkIdempotency` as the new **first** step (before `validate`), so a replay short-circuits ahead of the duplicate check.\n- Added `recordIdempotency` right after `save`, once the owner has a generated id.\n\n**Function classes** (`rest/function/owner/`)\n- `IdempotencyStore` \u2014 a `@Component` holding a `ConcurrentMap<String,Integer>` (key \u2192 owner id), with `find`/`record`.\n- `CheckIdempotency` \u2014 reads `@RequestHeader(name=\"Idempotency-Key\", required=false)`, republishes it as `Out<String>` for the recorder, and on an already-seen key loads the owner, maps it to a DTO (while the persistence context is open), and throws `IdempotentReplayException`. It deliberately does not read the body, leaving that to `ValidateOwnerFields`.\n- `RecordIdempotency` \u2014 remembers `key \u2192 owner.getId()` after save; a no-op when no key was sent.\n\n**Escalation** (`rest/escalation/` + `officefloor/escalation/\u2026IdempotentReplayException.yml`)\n- `IdempotentReplayException` carries the already-mapped `OwnerDto`; `IdempotentReplayExceptionHandler` responds `200 OK` with it \u2014 the sanctioned OfficeFloor way to short-circuit a pipeline and respond.\n\nRequests without the header are entirely unaffected (they flow straight through to the normal create), which the other 61 tests confirm.\n\nOne design note worth flagging: the store is in-memory (per JVM), which is exactly what the test needs and keeps the change self-contained. If you later want idempotency to survive restarts or span multiple instances, it should be backed by a persistent table instead \u2014 say the word and I'll convert it.",
