    "probe_text": "Read complete. Here is the full ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, as the code actually stands. Every step runs inside one shared transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`) that commits once at the end. I've marked each item **[V]** validation (can reject) or **[S]** side-effect (mutates/records).\n\n## Gate\n\n0. **[V] Authorization** (`composition.authorize`) \u2014 caller must have `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`, else the request is denied before any step runs.\n\n## Pipeline (in execution order)\n\n1. **CheckIdempotency**\n   - **[V/S] Idempotency replay** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key was already used and its owner still exists, it throws `IdempotentReplayException` and the original owner is replayed with **200**, short-circuiting the whole pipeline (this happens *before* the duplicate check could return 409).\n   - **[S]** Otherwise republishes the key (possibly null/blank) as a variable for later recording. Does **not** read the body.\n\n2. **ValidateOwnerFields** (the only step that binds `@RequestBody`) \u2014 collects all failures into one `MissingFieldsException` \u2192 **400** with an `errors` array:\n   - **[V]** `firstName` required (non-blank).\n   - **[V]** `lastName` required (non-blank).\n   - **[V] Address required** \u2014 either structured (`addressLine1` + optional `addressLine2`) or flat `address`; neither present \u2192 error on `address`.\n   - **[S] Address normalized & composed** \u2014 structured form preferred when `addressLine1` non-blank; stored `address` becomes normalized `addressLine1` + space + normalized `addressLine2` (or just line1), else the normalized flat `address`; `addressLine2` cleared when absent.\n   - **[V]** `city` required (non-blank).\n   - **[V/S] Telephone** \u2014 normalized to E.164 (strips spaces/dashes/brackets; assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0` when no `+`; result must be 8\u201315 digits; `+61`\u21d2exactly 9 national digits, `+1`\u21d2exactly 10). Unparseable \u2192 error on `telephone`; otherwise the normalized value replaces the input.\n   - **[V/S] Email** (only if present) \u2014 trimmed + lower-cased; must match the syntactic pattern; domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); invalid or disposable \u2192 error on `email`; otherwise stored lower-cased.\n   - **[V/S] Postcode** (only if present) \u2014 trimmed; must be exactly 4 digits **and** fall within the city's region range (`NSW 2000\u20132099`, `VIC 3000\u20133099`, `QLD 4000\u20134099`; unknown region accepts any 4-digit); malformed/out-of-range \u2192 error on `postcode`; otherwise stored trimmed.\n   - **[V]** `registrationDate` (only if present) \u2014 must not be later than the server's current date, else error on `registrationDate`.\n   - **[S]** Republishes the validated/normalized body for downstream steps.\n\n3. **EnsureCityCapacity** \u2014 **[V]** counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed); \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n4. **EnsureDailyLimit** \u2014 **[V]** counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today's business-day-adjusted date; \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyLimitException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n5. **BuildOwner** \u2014 **[S]** maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity; sets `registrationDate` (supplied value or default `today`) rolled forward to the next business day (skips weekends and the fixed 2026 holidays).\n\n6. **AssignHousehold** \u2014 **[S]** if a postcode is present, sets `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName|postcode`; no postcode \u21d2 `householdId` left null.\n\n7. **EnsureUniqueIdentity** \u2014 **[V]** the consolidated duplicate check (ignoring soft-deleted owners), \u2192 **409** `DuplicateIdentityException` when either:\n   - the full `identityKey` (`normalizedTelephone|email|householdId`) exactly matches an existing owner's; **or**\n   - the computed `householdId` matches an existing owner's (same lastName + postcode) \u2014 **unless** the request sets `sharesHousehold: true`.\n\n8. **AssignHouseholdSize** \u2014 **[S]** sets `householdSize` = existing members with the same `householdId` + 1 (1 when no household).\n\n9. **AssignCustomerCode** \u2014 **[S]** sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; HASH8 = first 8 upper hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`), appending `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 to resolve collisions with existing codes.\n\n10. **AssignNamesakeCount** \u2014 **[S]** sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing firstName + lastName (case-insensitive).\n\n11. **AssignBulkSignupWarning** \u2014 **[S]** sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true when > 80 owners already registered on today's business-day date.\n\n12. **AssignPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 **[S]** soft-match flag: if `sharesHousehold` is true, clears the flag; otherwise, for owners with a postcode, sets `possibleDuplicate` true and `possibleDuplicateOf` = the earliest (lowest-id) non-deleted existing owner that shares lastName + postcode but has a *different* telephone; else clears both.\n\n13. **SaveOwner** \u2014 **[S]** persists the owner (generates its id).\n\n14. **RecordIdempotency** \u2014 **[S]** if the request carried a non-blank `Idempotency-Key`, records key \u2192 new owner id, so future repeats replay this owner.\n\n15. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 **[S]** logs an `AUDIT` line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, derived membershipLevel and membershipNumber.\n\n16. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 **[S]** maps to `OwnerDto` and returns **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n\n## Notes on ordering that the code deliberately encodes\n- Idempotency replay is checked **first**, so a repeated request returns 200 rather than a 409.\n- Field validation runs **before** the capacity/limit/duplicate checks, so a malformed body is a 400 rather than being masked.\n- `EnsureUniqueIdentity` runs **after